---
// Approved Living Systems composition; native Astro, no client framework.
import PaperCta from '../ui/PaperCta.astro';
---
<section class="ls-manifesto-chapter" id="practice">
<header class="ls-chapter-heading ls-container">
<p class="ls-eyebrow">03 / The practice</p>
<h2>A DOCUMENT CAN HOLD <span class="ls-stroke">A PRACTICE.</span>
</h2>
</header>
<div class="ls-story-unit" data-tone="paper">
<div class="ls-container">
<div class="ls-principle-pair">
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="research">
<span class="ls-principle-index">09 /</span>
<h3>KEEP A WATCHFUL BRIEF.</h3>
<p>Point a competitor brief at a few public sources. Let Night Shift notice a change and refresh declared parts. Return to the passage, the evidence and your own notes. Pick up the argument where the world moved it.</p>
</article>
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="data">
<span class="ls-principle-index">10 /</span>
<h3>LET THE NUMBERS REDRAW.</h3>
<p>A budget or status report can bind its tables and charts to data. When the input changes, the view can follow. Keep the visual, its definition and the underlying numbers together, so the result is easier to question.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div class="ls-story-visual">
<figure aria-label="One document. Many ways to think." class="ls-scene ls-workshop-scene" data-frame="0" data-scene="true" data-scene-count="3">
<div class="ls-scene-chrome">
<span>
<i>
</i>
<i>
</i>
<i>
</i>
</span>
<b>One document. Many ways to think.</b>
<span>FLOW / ILLUSTRATION</span>
</div>
<div class="ls-scene-body">
<div aria-label="Document views" class="ls-scene-choice">
<button aria-pressed="true" data-scene-select="0" type="button">Table</button>
<button aria-pressed="false" data-scene-select="1" type="button">Chart</button>
<button aria-pressed="false" data-scene-select="2" type="button">Diagram</button>
</div>
<div class="ls-workshop-layout">
<div class="ls-code-sheet">
<span>SOURCE / PLAIN TEXT</span>
