<div class="ls-story-unit" data-tone="white" data-watermark="book">
<div class="ls-container">
<div class="ls-principle-pair">
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="notes">
<span class="ls-principle-index">11 /</span>
<h3>GIVE THE NEXT MORNING A START.</h3>
<p>A local model can turn gathered data into Overnight notes. Read them against the numbers and follow the question they raise. The routine prepares a starting point. What you make of it is where your experience, curiosity and imagination enter.</p>
</article>
<article class="ls-principle" data-principle="true" id="small">
<span class="ls-principle-index">12 /</span>
<h3>BEGIN WITH ONE RESPONSIBILITY.</h3>
<p>Choose a page you actually reopen. Define one useful job in the editor. Run it once, inspect the result, then give it a rhythm. A small routine that earns repeat use matters more than a sweeping promise.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div class="ls-story-visual">
<figure aria-label="One responsibility, carried through" class="ls-scene ls-one-note-scene" data-frame="0" data-scene="true" data-scene-count="3">
