<path d="M20.985 12.486a9 9 0 1 1-9.473-9.472c.405-.022.617.46.402.803a6 6 0 0 0 8.268 8.268c.344-.215.825-.004.803.401">
</path>
</svg> OVERNIGHT NOTE / LOCAL MODEL</span>
<div data-scene-panel="0">
<h3>First, the numbers.</h3>
<p>The source update reports six of eight launch tasks complete. The bound table is refreshed.</p>
<small>Gather → redraw the declared view</small>
</div>
<div data-scene-panel="1" hidden="">
<h3>Then, a useful starting point.</h3>
<p>“Launch is now six of eight tasks complete, up from four. Two fewer tasks remain.”</p>
<small>Illustrative model note · Pro required</small>
</div>
<div data-scene-panel="2" hidden="">
<h3>Now, your judgment.</h3>
<p>Read the note against its source. Keep it, or restore this part. Your next question is yours to choose.</p>
<small>Marked change → Morning Briefing</small>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p class="ls-scene-note">Sample workflow. Deterministic gathering and redraw are Base; model-powered notes are Pro. Start with one job you understand.</p>
</div>
